# What `podman build -f deploy/Containerfile .` may send as its build context (spec 0218, R2.4).
#
# Podman reads this file from the context directory, which is the repository root, so it lives
# here and not under deploy/ (design review F3). The image holds code and dbt's project and
# nothing else: no credential, no landing zone, no warehouse, no history. The units mount the
# ESPN `.env` and the Google key at run time. tests/test_deploy_files.py reads this file.

# credentials
.env
*.env
**/.env
**/*.env
secrets
**/secrets
*.pem
*.p12
**/*service-account*.json
**/*google-key*.json
**/fo-key-*.json
**/application_default_credentials.json

# the real season and every warehouse
data
**/*.duckdb
**/*.duckdb.wal
**/*.duckdb.tmp

# not needed to run, and large or private
.git
.review
.venv
site
docs
fixtures
dashboard
**/__pycache__
dbt/target
dbt/logs
dbt/dbt_packages
